[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1955417070","pull_request_review_id":2616533242,"id":1955417070,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc50jUvu","diff_hunk":"@@ -5218,12 +5218,12 @@ Size2i SubViewport::get_size() const {\n \n void SubViewport::set_size_2d_override(const Size2i &p_size) {\n \tERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD;\n-\t_set_size(_get_size(), p_size, true);\n+\t_set_size(_get_size(), Size2(p_size), true);\n }\n \n Size2i SubViewport::get_size_2d_override() const {\n \tERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(Size2i());\n-\treturn _get_size_2d_override();\n+\treturn Size2i(_get_size_2d_override());","path":"scene/main/viewport.cpp","commit_id":"315cc5e4375e0eb21c083b33f6759e85714fc689","original_commit_id":"0c53a482fb2fe4d4572f7470b6d21063c4f2809b","user":{"login":"OhiraKyou","id":7255919,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTU5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7255919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou","html_url":"https://github.com/OhiraKyou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'm assuming this results in float to int truncation (e.g., `1.9` being truncated to `1` instead of rounded to `2`). In my experience, setting a viewport's size from a float vector requires explicit rounding to prevent incorrect results caused by truncation. See my script [here](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/77149#issuecomment-1813783014) for an example of when this was needed from gdscript to achieve correct results while scaling a SubViewport. So, I imagine getting accurate values would require rounding in this case too.","created_at":"2025-02-14T01:04:33Z","updated_at":"2025-02-14T04:20:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1955417070","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1955417070"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1955417070"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1955417070/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":5226,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":42,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1956013187","pull_request_review_id":2617545607,"id":1956013187,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc50lmSD","diff_hunk":"@@ -5218,12 +5218,12 @@ Size2i SubViewport::get_size() const {\n \n void SubViewport::set_size_2d_override(const Size2i &p_size) {\n \tERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD;\n-\t_set_size(_get_size(), p_size, true);\n+\t_set_size(_get_size(), Size2(p_size), true);\n }\n \n Size2i SubViewport::get_size_2d_override() const {\n \tERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(Size2i());\n-\treturn _get_size_2d_override();\n+\treturn Size2i(_get_size_2d_override());","path":"scene/main/viewport.cpp","commit_id":"315cc5e4375e0eb21c083b33f6759e85714fc689","original_commit_id":"0c53a482fb2fe4d4572f7470b6d21063c4f2809b","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I was thinking along the lines of there's no public way to set this value to a non-integer equivalent, so rounding is not necessary, but you are right, it's probably better to round here just in case the engine uses the protected `_set_size()` method somewhere.\r\n\r\nHonestly I'd just want to expose this all the way through so you could set pixel-correct subviewport sizes from the user side, but changing the type of the property seems to be a comp break. Do you know if there's a way to handle this with some compatibility getter-setters or something?\r\n\r\nIf not, I've pushed a commit with your suggested change and a comment.","created_at":"2025-02-14T11:40:34Z","updated_at":"2025-02-14T12:43:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1956013187","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1956013187"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1956013187"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1956013187/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":5226,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1955417070,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":42,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1957108038","pull_request_review_id":2619398192,"id":1957108038,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc50pxlG","diff_hunk":"@@ -5218,12 +5218,12 @@ Size2i SubViewport::get_size() const {\n \n void SubViewport::set_size_2d_override(const Size2i &p_size) {\n \tERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD;\n-\t_set_size(_get_size(), p_size, true);\n+\t_set_size(_get_size(), Size2(p_size), true);\n }\n \n Size2i SubViewport::get_size_2d_override() const {\n \tERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(Size2i());\n-\treturn _get_size_2d_override();\n+\treturn Size2i(_get_size_2d_override());","path":"scene/main/viewport.cpp","commit_id":"315cc5e4375e0eb21c083b33f6759e85714fc689","original_commit_id":"0c53a482fb2fe4d4572f7470b6d21063c4f2809b","user":{"login":"OhiraKyou","id":7255919,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTU5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7255919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou","html_url":"https://github.com/OhiraKyou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I haven't worked with the editor code itself. So, I can't be of much help there. That said, data serialization might complicate compatibility beyond script binding.\r\n\r\nIncidentally, some research I've done since suggests that the round function may have some subtle quirks that can be avoided by adding half a vector and flooring instead. [This code search](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agodotengine%2Fgodot+is_snap_2d_transforms_to_pixel_enabled&type=code) reveals that various classes use that.\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvalue = (value + Vector2(0.5, 0.5)).floor();\r\n```","created_at":"2025-02-15T12:32:41Z","updated_at":"2025-02-15T12:32:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1957108038","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1957108038"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1957108038"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1957108038/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":5226,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1955417070,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":42,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1957943990","pull_request_review_id":2620572002,"id":1957943990,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc50s9q2","diff_hunk":"@@ -5218,12 +5218,12 @@ Size2i SubViewport::get_size() const {\n \n void SubViewport::set_size_2d_override(const Size2i &p_size) {\n \tERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD;\n-\t_set_size(_get_size(), p_size, true);\n+\t_set_size(_get_size(), Size2(p_size), true);\n }\n \n Size2i SubViewport::get_size_2d_override() const {\n \tERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(Size2i());\n-\treturn _get_size_2d_override();\n+\treturn Size2i(_get_size_2d_override());","path":"scene/main/viewport.cpp","commit_id":"315cc5e4375e0eb21c083b33f6759e85714fc689","original_commit_id":"0c53a482fb2fe4d4572f7470b6d21063c4f2809b","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Math::round (that Vector2.round() calls internally) is also used in the window class for calculating projections, and in a bunch of other places in the code. What in particular is wrong with it?\r\n\r\nShouldn't we fix the entire function then instead of adding workarounds everywhere we want to use it?\r\n\r\n(I've updated it, just curious.)","created_at":"2025-02-17T09:59:36Z","updated_at":"2025-02-17T10:11:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1957943990","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1957943990"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1957943990"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1957943990/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":5226,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1955417070,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":42,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1958219544","pull_request_review_id":2621043356,"id":1958219544,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc50uA8Y","diff_hunk":"@@ -5218,12 +5218,12 @@ Size2i SubViewport::get_size() const {\n \n void SubViewport::set_size_2d_override(const Size2i &p_size) {\n \tERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD;\n-\t_set_size(_get_size(), p_size, true);\n+\t_set_size(_get_size(), Size2(p_size), true);\n }\n \n Size2i SubViewport::get_size_2d_override() const {\n \tERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(Size2i());\n-\treturn _get_size_2d_override();\n+\treturn Size2i(_get_size_2d_override());","path":"scene/main/viewport.cpp","commit_id":"315cc5e4375e0eb21c083b33f6759e85714fc689","original_commit_id":"0c53a482fb2fe4d4572f7470b6d21063c4f2809b","user":{"login":"OhiraKyou","id":7255919,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyNTU5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7255919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou","html_url":"https://github.com/OhiraKyou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/OhiraKyou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Rounding is biased away from zero. As a result, you can get some unexpected pixel distances anywhere negative values are allowed.\r\n\r\nFor example, the following results in 2 instead of the expected 1:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nfloat difference = std::round(0.5) - std::round(-0.5);\r\n\r\n// Prints \"The difference between round(-0.5) and round(0.5) is 2\"\r\nstd::cout << \"The difference between round(-0.5) and round(0.5) is \" << difference << std::endl;\r\n```\r\n\r\nSnapping by adding `0.5` and flooring is distributed uniformly and would print a difference of `1` in that case. But, it's only relevant when negative values are allowed to be assigned. And, negative values are allowed for `SubViewport` size overrides.\r\n\r\nGiven its name, I would expect [Math::round](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/93d270693079ea7802c9e1334a2e0ecd8529eeed/core/math/math_funcs.h#L508-L509) to be a direct wrapper that returns `-1` when given `-0.5`, `-2` when given `-1.5`, etc. So, I wouldn't change the base `round` function. And, although this is speculation, leaving the offset and flooring inline (rather than in a new utility function) could have been an intentional decision to make the math being used clear at a glance.","created_at":"2025-02-17T13:14:36Z","updated_at":"2025-02-17T13:18:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1958219544","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1958219544"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102741#discussion_r1958219544"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/102741"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1958219544/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":5226,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":1955417070,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":42,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/1959434027","pull_request_review_id":2623037945,"id":1959434027,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc50ypcr","diff_hunk":"@@ -5218,12 +5218,12 @@ Size2i SubViewport::get_size() const {\n \n void SubViewport::set_size_2d_override(const Size2i &p_size) {\n \tERR_MAIN_THREAD_GUARD;\n-\t_set_size(_get_size(), p_size, true);\n+\t_set_size(_get_size(), Size2(p_size), true);\n }\n \n Size2i SubViewport::get_size_2d_override() const {\n \tERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(Size2i());\n-\treturn _get_size_2d_override();\n+\treturn Size2i(_get_size_2d_override());","path":"scene/main/viewport.cpp","commit_id":"315cc5e4375e0eb21c083b33f6759e85714fc689","original_commit_id":"0c53a482fb2fe4d4572f7470b6d21063c4f2809b","user":{"login":"KerekesDavid","id":9087461,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwODc0NjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9087461?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid","html_url":"https://github.com/KerekesDavid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KerekesDavid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.co